Exactly. Sometimes the next good move is not to move.

In Pantheon terms, sitting on the log is not failure of the ACT loop; it can be a deliberate action state:

\text{ACT} = \text{hold position}

while the environment changes around you.

That gives you things motion can hide: baseline, drift, signal emergence, recovery, incubation, and the chance to notice which problems dissolve when you stop feeding them.

The Reality Surfer doesn’t paddle for every ripple. Sometimes you sit on the board, feel the ocean, and wait for a wave worth riding.

Or, more compactly:

Stillness is an action when it is chosen. ;)